     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m generating model-based predictions from an N-mixture model (pcount) in unmarked using the predict function.  The predictions are set up so that all other variables aside from the one of interest are held at their null value (0 - all covariates were standardized to zero before modeling).  My predicted SE and generated confidence intervals seem awfully narrow to me though...has anyone else encountered this?  I&#39;ve included an example below of the abundance covariates predicted across different values.  The table shows the parameter estimates from the model.  <div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d82xu1_ChzU/VNj0BioMJII/AAAAAAAAAGg/9r9qfZ75JD8/s1600/Part2.jpg\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d82xu1_ChzU/VNj0BioMJII/AAAAAAAAAGg/9r9qfZ75JD8/s1600/Part2.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792453129439000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0fUNegRgbtQK67m66eRp4U\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-d82xu1_ChzU/VNj0BioMJII/AAAAAAAAAGg/9r9qfZ75JD8/s320/Part2.jpg\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"174\"></a></p><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"320\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:240pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"64\" span=\"5\" style=\"width:48pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"128\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:96pt\">Abundance:</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\"></td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\"></td>\r\n  <td>Estimate</td>\r\n  <td>SE</td>\r\n  <td>z</td>\r\n  <td>P(&gt;|z|)</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r