     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:Verdana;color:#000000;font-size:10pt\">\r\nDear Kaylan,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nthe prediction SE will be a function of the SE of the parameter estimates that go into that prediction, and these seem pretty small, too, for some reason. So you seem lucky in that everything is estimated highly precisely and hence, with a small SE.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nActually, I wonder whether there is perhaps some hidden pseudoreplication ? What&#39;s the number of sites and reps in your analysis ?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nRegards  --  Marc<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Times New Roman;color:#000000;font-size:16px\">\r\n<hr>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"2\" face=\"Tahoma\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a> [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a>] on behalf of Kaylan [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">k.ke...@gmail.com</a>]<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 09 February 2015 18:55<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">unma...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [unmarked] unmarked and predict - confidence intervals<br>\r\n</font><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div></div></div></div></div>"
